{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>And He shone from Seir</b> Three times in the Masorah: וזרח משעיר, וזרח בחשך, וזרח השמש. וזרח משעיר — He revealed Himself to Esau to receive the Torah but they did not want to; therefore וזרח בחשך — they were punished and it turned for them to darkness and gloom. But Israel, who received it — וזרח השמש. As stated: \"The commandment of YHWH is clear, enlightening the eyes.\"" "<b>He appeared</b> Three times: הופיא מהר פארן; מציון מכלל יופי אלהים הופיע; אל נקמות ה' אל נקמות הופיע — [for the nations]. But Israel, who received it, merited what is stated: מציון מכלל יופי אלהים הופיע." "<b>Of myriads</b> Two times: ואתה מרבבות קדש; לא אירא מרבבות עם. Why? כי אתה ה' מרבבות קדש — to help me."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 33, :notes {1 "The bracketed [לאומות] appears in the source; kept as found. The first quotation reads הופיא (defective) rather than הופיע, preserved as in the Hebrew."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:11:24.850114198Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}